# Build context exclusions: keep the image small and deterministic.
#
# The Dockerfile copies the whole repository (`COPY . /opt/ergane`) and does an
# editable install.  These entries protect the build from host state that is not
# part of the committed distribution:
#
# - `.git` is large and unnecessary after the tag is baked into the version.
# - `.venv` on the host may point at a foreign interpreter (e.g. aarch64 CPython
#   3.13 under `~/.local/share/uv/`); copying it without `--clear` then running
#   `python3 -m venv .venv` with Ubuntu's python3.12 produces a broken mix.
# - `.factory` and `.claude` hold attempt and worktree state.
# - `.ergane` and `.temporal` are runtime roots the ENGINE ITSELF creates inside
#   the repository, and omitting them was a credential leak, not a size problem.
#   `.ergane/homes/<spec>/<node>/.claude/.credentials.json` is a real Claude Code
#   credential per dispatched node, retained for every spec ever run; a local
#   `docker build` copied all of them into the image. Measured on this tree
#   2026-08-26: `.ergane` 11G (47 spec homes), `.temporal/dev.db` 1.8G, against a
#   457MB published image. CI never saw it because `actions/checkout@v4` produces
#   a clean clone — so the published images are unaffected and only the LOCAL
#   build path, the one a rehearsal and a brownfield container install both take,
#   was exposed.
# - `dist`, `build`, `**/__pycache__` and `*.egg-info` are build residue.
#
# This list is a deny-list guarding against directories created by the very
# program it ships, which is a losing shape: the next runtime root added will be
# absent here too, and the failure is silent. Inverting it to an allow-list is
# the real fix and wants a spec.
#
# Must NOT exclude files the wheel needs:
# - `pyproject.toml` and `README.md` are required by `readme = "README.md"`.
# - `personas.example.yaml` is force-included into the wheel as
#   `factory/personas.yaml`.
# - `factory/` is the package itself.
.git
.venv
.factory
.claude
.ergane
.temporal
dist
build
**/__pycache__
*.egg-info
